/**
 * sweep — remove the run roots under `bin/.tkrun/` that are neither `keep` nor still held by a live
 * process (§2.2).
 *
 * THE CLEANUP IS THE NEXT RUN'S, NEVER ITS OWN. A run that cleaned on exit would lose the cleanup in
 * the one case it matters (abrupt death) and lose with it the proof that it died. Sweeping on OPEN
 * has the opposite property: a `SIGKILL` leaves the root ON PURPOSE, and the next run reclaims it
 * only after it could have reported it — and only once its locker is gone.
 *
 * @param keep  the run root to preserve (this run's own)
 * @return      how many roots were removed
 * @since 0.3.1
 */
pub fn sweep(keep: str) -> u64 { sweep_under(TKRUN_DIR, keep) }
